    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nIn visual mode, running this mapping:\n```lua\nvim.keymap.set(\"x\", \"gt\", function()\n  vim.api.nvim_buf_set_extmark(\n    0,\n    vim.api.nvim_create_namespace(\"nvim.multicursor.visual\"),\n    0,\n    0,\n    { end_row = 0, end_col = 2 }\n  )\n  vim.print(vim.api.nvim_buf_get_extmarks(0, visual_ns, 0, -1))\nend)\n```\nThe extmarks are updated, but it doesn't create a new visual selection. And upon exiting visual mode, the newly placed multicursor isn't there in normal mode.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nSimilar to how you can set cursors in normal mode via `nvim.multicursor`, it would be possible to use `nvim.multicursor.visual` to do the same in visual mode.\n\nMy personal usecase for this is a binding to rotate selections, where each cursor also moves to the next cursor's position.",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
